{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/arrowDown","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/arrowUp","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/doubleSharp","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/doubleSharpDown","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLA